8
00:04:47,986 --> 00:04:56,826
It was my first day as a high school junior.

9
00:04:58,706 --> 00:05:00,586
Everyone, take a seat.

10
00:05:01,866 --> 00:05:05,686
I knew Brother was starting his new job here, but this couldn't be happening.

11
00:05:07,066 --> 00:05:09,506
I never imagined he would be my homeroom teacher.

12
00:05:11,346 --> 00:05:12,766
I was so happy.

13
00:05:14,866 --> 00:05:17,526
I would be able to see him every day at school.

14
00:05:17,986 --> 00:05:31,386
Hey, Mr. Kanai!

15
00:05:33,526 --> 00:05:35,206
I'm not going to do this.

16
00:05:36,426 --> 00:05:39,066
Ah, Mr. Kanai, one of your students.

17
00:05:39,726 --> 00:05:42,446
Oh, you brought me the handouts. Thanks.

18
00:05:42,446 --> 00:05:48,866
It's been a long time that I've been watching you, Brother.

19
00:05:50,866 --> 00:05:53,786
That's why I noticed him making a face before he did.

20
00:05:56,266 --> 00:05:58,186
One I've never seen him make before.

21
00:05:58,186 --> 00:06:01,446
I'm so stupid.

22
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,006
I let my guard down.

23
00:06:05,486 --> 00:06:08,966
I can't believe that stupid little middle-aged chick could wiggle herself in there!

24
00:06:09,146 --> 00:06:09,326
Huh?

25
00:06:09,326 --> 00:06:23,486
You know, I can't believe how much Hana has mellowed out.

26
00:06:24,046 --> 00:06:24,446
Really?

27
00:06:25,146 --> 00:06:27,666
She's just being polite because you're here, sweetie.

28
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:30,506
Please, Mom, chill.

29
00:06:30,846 --> 00:06:31,946
Yeah, yeah.

30
00:06:31,946 --> 00:06:34,506
Ah, delicious.

31
00:06:35,986 --> 00:06:36,546
Obviously.

32
00:06:37,086 --> 00:06:40,206
You're so lucky your mother has always been such a good cook.

33
00:06:40,866 --> 00:06:42,406
That's very kind of you, dear.

34
00:06:42,786 --> 00:06:45,046
But Hana actually helped me out this time around.

35
00:06:45,286 --> 00:06:46,826
She almost never does that.

36
00:06:47,066 --> 00:06:48,766
Mom, stop it!

37
00:06:49,026 --> 00:06:52,046
Well, regardless, it turned out to be very delicious.

38
00:06:52,046 --> 00:06:54,806
I'm so angry.

39
00:06:55,346 --> 00:06:57,146
Thanks again for the wonderful meal.

40
00:06:57,186 --> 00:07:00,126
To think I feel so saved by such a meaningless little thing.

41
00:07:01,206 --> 00:07:03,086
Even though it's pointless to hope.

42
00:07:03,266 --> 00:07:04,586
We're neighbors, after all.

43
00:07:08,086 --> 00:07:09,906
Homemade cooking is the best.

44
00:07:10,466 --> 00:07:12,646
It's only me and Pops at home, you know.

45
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:14,946
Neither of us can really cook.

46
00:07:16,726 --> 00:07:18,186
I need one soon.

47
00:07:18,186 --> 00:07:19,106
Hmm.

48
00:07:20,046 --> 00:07:20,326
Hmm.

49
00:07:22,046 --> 00:07:23,366
Here he goes.

50
00:07:23,726 --> 00:07:25,586
I can't wait to have a wonderful wife.

51
00:07:26,786 --> 00:07:28,286
It's something he always says.

52
00:07:29,766 --> 00:07:31,926
He's been saying it ever since junior high.

53
00:07:32,366 --> 00:07:33,786
But lately he hasn't bothered.

54
00:07:35,126 --> 00:07:36,186
Is that...

55
00:07:37,186 --> 00:07:39,866
Because he now has someone specific in mind?

56
00:07:49,266 --> 00:07:50,626
That's amazing, Hana!

57
00:07:50,806 --> 00:07:52,006
You got first place!

58
00:07:52,046 --> 00:07:52,746
That's awesome!

59
00:07:53,006 --> 00:07:53,926
I'm so jealous!

60
00:07:55,146 --> 00:07:55,526
Hey!

61
00:07:56,706 --> 00:07:59,406
Why didn't you run with your actual mom or dad, Hana-bee?

62
00:08:00,706 --> 00:08:01,026
Huh?

63
00:08:01,786 --> 00:08:02,326
Yeah!

64
00:08:02,506 --> 00:08:03,146
You're right!

65
00:08:03,266 --> 00:08:04,226
He's too young!

66
00:08:04,346 --> 00:08:05,486
That's not her dad!

67
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:07,626
Totally unfair!

68
00:08:08,366 --> 00:08:08,806
Cheater!

69
00:08:09,286 --> 00:08:09,766
Cheater!

70
00:08:10,266 --> 00:08:10,626
Cheater!

71
00:08:10,786 --> 00:08:11,906
Stop that, Norco!

72
00:08:13,906 --> 00:08:14,506
Hana.

73
00:08:14,506 --> 00:08:17,026
Shut up.

74
00:08:17,826 --> 00:08:18,226
Huh?

75
00:08:18,226 --> 00:08:20,286
You know what's really unfair?

76
00:08:20,506 --> 00:08:21,686
Your stupid shoes!

77
00:08:23,906 --> 00:08:24,506
Hey!

78
00:08:24,806 --> 00:08:25,666
Hana-bee's right!

79
00:08:25,966 --> 00:08:26,606
Hold on!

80
00:08:26,686 --> 00:08:30,246
They told us we weren't allowed to wear those types of speed shoes during the races!

81
00:08:31,646 --> 00:08:33,086
Is that true, Norco?

82
00:08:33,446 --> 00:08:35,066
What did you get yourself into?

83
00:08:38,066 --> 00:08:38,626
Hana?

84
00:08:39,626 --> 00:08:40,926
Come on, Hana.

85
00:08:40,926 --> 00:08:41,466
Uh...

86
00:08:41,466 --> 00:08:42,806
Hey there.

87
00:08:45,546 --> 00:08:46,906
I don't really care.

88
00:08:47,886 --> 00:08:48,126
Hmm?

89
00:08:49,006 --> 00:08:50,566
Running with you isn't unfair.

90
00:08:50,966 --> 00:08:52,366
Norco's just a sore loser.

91
00:08:53,626 --> 00:08:54,346
That's right.

92
00:08:54,346 --> 00:09:02,346
Let's not forget, it's also not unfair for me to eat the lunch your mother packed for

93
00:09:02,346 --> 00:09:02,826
you to have.

94
00:09:03,266 --> 00:09:03,746
Really?

95
00:09:04,406 --> 00:09:06,406
Mom said she had to work all day today!

96
00:09:07,086 --> 00:09:12,426
She stayed up late to make this for you, so then we should probably eat it all.

97
00:09:12,746 --> 00:09:13,106
Okay!

98
00:09:15,606 --> 00:09:16,086
It's...

99
00:09:16,086 --> 00:09:17,206
so good!

100
00:09:17,626 --> 00:09:19,146
This is just average.

101
00:09:19,146 --> 00:09:27,306
Hana, someday you will appreciate having a mother that can cook for you.

102
00:09:27,546 --> 00:09:30,346
Maybe you're right, but you went fishing with your father.

103
00:09:30,746 --> 00:09:30,946
Hmm?

104
00:09:31,926 --> 00:09:34,266
I don't have a dad I can go fish with.

105
00:09:34,946 --> 00:09:36,566
You make me feel jealous.

106
00:09:37,426 --> 00:09:38,286
I understand.

107
00:09:41,866 --> 00:09:46,266
Well, then it looks like we both have something the other is jealous of.

108
00:09:47,506 --> 00:09:48,706
That's good, I guess.

109
00:09:48,706 --> 00:09:51,446
We can help each other when we feel lonely.

110
00:10:07,966 --> 00:10:08,446
Fire!

111
00:10:08,446 --> 00:10:08,606
Fire!

112
00:10:08,606 --> 00:10:08,666
Fire!

113
00:10:18,706 --> 00:10:21,226
Miss Minagawa's so friggin' hot.

114
00:10:21,326 --> 00:10:22,306
The new music teacher?

115
00:10:22,686 --> 00:10:23,706
She's not old either.

116
00:10:24,186 --> 00:10:25,546
She's close to our age, right?

117
00:10:25,926 --> 00:10:26,086
Huh?

118
00:10:26,486 --> 00:10:29,086
Hey, is that Hanabi looking at us over there?

119
00:10:29,766 --> 00:10:30,246
Really?

120
00:10:30,586 --> 00:10:31,546
Is she looking at me?

121
00:10:31,806 --> 00:10:32,586
Don't be stupid.

122
00:10:32,746 --> 00:10:33,226
It's me.

123
00:10:34,666 --> 00:10:34,946
Oh!

124
00:10:34,946 --> 00:10:35,266
Oh!

125
00:10:36,066 --> 00:10:36,366
Oh!

126
00:10:37,266 --> 00:10:37,746
Oh!

127
00:10:38,746 --> 00:10:40,106
I'm so sorry!

128
00:10:40,766 --> 00:10:41,846
Are you injured?

129
00:10:42,446 --> 00:10:43,546
Are you okay there?

130
00:10:43,546 --> 00:10:46,826
Long length hair.

131
00:10:47,306 --> 00:10:48,526
Lame beige cardigan.

132
00:10:49,126 --> 00:10:51,166
Strong smell of boring old people shampoo.

133
00:10:51,906 --> 00:10:53,486
Natural style basic makeup.

134
00:10:57,286 --> 00:11:02,046
Here you go, Miss Minagawa.

135
00:11:03,086 --> 00:11:03,966
Thank you, dear.

136
00:11:04,186 --> 00:11:05,566
You're sweet, Mugi.

137
00:11:05,566 --> 00:11:07,466
We're at school right now.

138
00:11:07,846 --> 00:11:08,486
Miss Minagawa.

139
00:11:09,086 --> 00:11:10,186
Oh, dearie me!

140
00:11:10,386 --> 00:11:11,026
That's right!

141
00:11:11,186 --> 00:11:12,006
Jeez, I've done it again!

142
00:11:12,006 --> 00:11:12,846
Who is this guy?

143
00:11:13,286 --> 00:11:14,786
Another one of her fanboys?

144
00:11:15,126 --> 00:11:16,466
I can't believe this is happening.

145
00:11:16,606 --> 00:11:17,146
How embarrassing!

146
00:11:17,326 --> 00:11:18,306
Please forgive me!

147
00:11:18,306 --> 00:11:18,526
Huh?

148
00:11:19,246 --> 00:11:19,706
No.

149
00:11:21,106 --> 00:11:22,446
I recognize that.

150
00:11:22,946 --> 00:11:24,006
The look in his eyes.

151
00:11:24,006 --> 00:11:26,526
Hey.

152
00:11:28,166 --> 00:11:28,726
Huh?

153
00:11:34,826 --> 00:11:37,706
I'm sorry, but do you know who she likes?

154
00:11:39,946 --> 00:11:40,726
I do.

155
00:11:43,966 --> 00:11:45,386
What a coincidence.

156
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:48,686
Akane was my tutor back when I was in junior high.

157
00:11:48,686 --> 00:11:53,646
I never would have thought she would actually become a teacher in my high school.

158
00:11:54,566 --> 00:11:57,306
At first, I thought I was really lucky to have her here.

159
00:12:00,706 --> 00:12:01,686
Are you listening?

160
00:12:03,326 --> 00:12:06,146
What's so special about a basic woman like her?

161
00:12:06,746 --> 00:12:08,926
Hey there, don't you dare go insulting Akane.

162
00:12:09,146 --> 00:12:09,986
Yeah, yeah.

163
00:12:10,226 --> 00:12:13,346
Guys like those sweet, sempering, doe-eyed girls, don't they?

164
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:16,226
They were both very vindictive people in our longing.

165
00:12:17,146 --> 00:12:17,726
Listen here!

166
00:12:17,926 --> 00:12:19,366
And the stronger we felt for them,

167
00:12:20,166 --> 00:12:22,126
the harder we moped.

168
00:12:24,006 --> 00:12:31,026
Before we knew what was happening,

169
00:12:31,806 --> 00:12:34,166
we were spending a lot of time with each other.

170
00:12:34,166 --> 00:12:39,586
Ugh, I'm so done with this whole thing.

171
00:12:40,046 --> 00:12:42,206
Hey, don't get my bed wet with your tears.

172
00:12:42,606 --> 00:12:45,126
I just want to quit school and never come back.

173
00:12:45,926 --> 00:12:47,486
You talking about Mr. Kanai?

174
00:12:47,846 --> 00:12:49,086
You're just going to give him up?

175
00:12:51,026 --> 00:12:52,426
I could never do that.

176
00:12:53,326 --> 00:12:53,766
But?

177
00:12:54,286 --> 00:12:54,946
But what?

178
00:12:54,946 --> 00:13:06,786
I was just messing around.

179
00:13:07,546 --> 00:13:08,866
At first, at least.

180
00:13:09,686 --> 00:13:09,986
Huh?

181
00:13:15,186 --> 00:13:16,286
You scared me.

182
00:13:17,206 --> 00:13:17,646
Really?

183
00:13:17,646 --> 00:13:19,266
I couldn't tell at all.

184
00:13:26,766 --> 00:13:27,626
You sad?

185
00:13:30,646 --> 00:13:32,186
Aren't you sad too, Mookie?

186
00:13:34,986 --> 00:13:36,206
It took some time.

187
00:13:37,166 --> 00:13:39,546
But I think we both were thinking the same thing.

188
00:13:39,546 --> 00:14:06,686
Mookie doesn't have any lustful feelings for me like that.

189
00:14:06,686 --> 00:14:10,406
Whether I see Mookie as Mookie or not,

190
00:14:11,086 --> 00:14:12,186
it doesn't matter.

191
00:14:13,446 --> 00:14:14,826
Hey, that tickles Mookie.

192
00:14:16,246 --> 00:14:17,206
In the end,

193
00:14:17,666 --> 00:14:19,346
I'm just a replacement too.

194
00:14:21,626 --> 00:14:23,406
Do you even want to do this?

195
00:14:25,126 --> 00:14:26,486
You're the one who wants to.

196
00:14:26,486 --> 00:14:28,786
But you look nothing like him.

197
00:14:30,066 --> 00:14:32,286
I don't know how you expect me to pretend.

198
00:14:33,086 --> 00:14:34,206
You're way too demanding.

199
00:14:35,126 --> 00:14:37,886
And I'm pretty good looking, you know?

200
00:14:47,226 --> 00:14:49,326
Just close your eyes.

201
00:14:49,326 --> 00:14:51,166
Yes.

202
00:14:51,966 --> 00:14:53,326
If we're going to do this,

203
00:14:53,506 --> 00:14:54,586
then we really do it.

204
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:04,906
Oh, crap.

205
00:15:05,386 --> 00:15:06,206
What is this?

206
00:15:06,886 --> 00:15:08,326
If I imagine that he's brother...

207
00:15:10,026 --> 00:15:11,346
My fingertips are cold.

208
00:15:12,146 --> 00:15:13,526
Everything feels so distant.

209
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:15,626
All I can hear is my heart.

210
00:15:15,626 --> 00:15:17,626
Because...

211
00:15:18,146 --> 00:15:21,986
This is what I've wanted from him.

212
00:15:23,386 --> 00:15:23,986
Forever.

213
00:15:31,926 --> 00:15:33,306
It was electric.

214
00:15:40,026 --> 00:15:42,806
Did you know that was my first kiss?

215
00:15:43,146 --> 00:15:43,766
No way.

216
00:15:43,766 --> 00:15:45,246
Really.

217
00:15:47,026 --> 00:15:48,126
It felt good.

218
00:15:53,386 --> 00:15:54,426
One more time.

219
00:16:07,146 --> 00:16:08,806
There's a part of me that worries.

220
00:16:08,806 --> 00:16:13,626
Am I really being a good enough replacement for him?

221
00:16:14,226 --> 00:16:15,086
Can he pretend?

222
00:16:28,966 --> 00:16:29,846
It's okay.

223
00:16:30,546 --> 00:16:30,806
These hands...

224
00:16:32,806 --> 00:16:33,806
Our brother's hands...

225
00:16:33,806 --> 00:16:35,806
I'm sorry.

226
00:16:35,806 --> 00:16:36,266
I'm sorry.

227
00:16:36,966 --> 00:16:38,186
I'm so sorry.

228
00:16:46,026 --> 00:16:49,826
The things brother doesn't do.

229
00:16:50,666 --> 00:16:52,366
The things he won't do for me.

230
00:16:53,866 --> 00:16:55,806
The things I want to do to him.

231
00:16:55,806 --> 00:17:15,706
I can't see his face.

232
00:17:16,166 --> 00:17:17,206
He's so quiet.

233
00:17:18,346 --> 00:17:20,266
I have to try to stay quiet, too.

234
00:17:20,266 --> 00:17:23,146
I don't want to remind him it's me.

235
00:17:24,346 --> 00:17:24,866
Concentrate.

236
00:17:25,486 --> 00:17:26,746
Don't betray him.

237
00:17:30,586 --> 00:17:31,106
Oh.

238
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:32,706
That's good.

239
00:17:33,706 --> 00:17:35,306
He can't see my face like this.

240
00:17:35,306 --> 00:17:39,746
I have to remember as much as possible.

241
00:17:42,086 --> 00:17:43,386
Hold on to it.

242
00:17:50,786 --> 00:17:51,346
Huh?

243
00:17:51,346 --> 00:17:55,006
Who could that be?

244
00:17:56,086 --> 00:17:56,386
Oh.

245
00:17:56,706 --> 00:17:57,386
I'm sorry.

246
00:17:58,826 --> 00:17:59,086
Ugh.

247
00:18:04,506 --> 00:18:05,066
Why?

248
00:18:09,466 --> 00:18:10,306
You done?

249
00:18:10,726 --> 00:18:11,046
Huh?

250
00:18:11,046 --> 00:18:13,066
Yeah.

251
00:18:13,746 --> 00:18:15,466
I think that'll be enough for us today.

252
00:18:16,386 --> 00:18:17,666
But, um...

253
00:18:17,666 --> 00:18:19,026
You want to keep doing this?

254
00:18:20,106 --> 00:18:20,906
Or stop?

255
00:18:31,626 --> 00:18:32,446
I'm sorry.

256
00:18:34,326 --> 00:18:35,126
I'm sorry.

257
00:18:35,826 --> 00:18:37,026
I gave you my answer.

258
00:18:37,626 --> 00:18:37,866
Goodbye.

259
00:18:38,346 --> 00:18:38,726
Huh?

260
00:18:39,506 --> 00:18:39,946
Wait.

261
00:18:41,566 --> 00:18:42,166
I...

262
00:18:42,166 --> 00:18:43,946
I waited a week for your answer.

263
00:18:44,826 --> 00:18:46,186
You can't just...

264
00:18:46,186 --> 00:18:47,006
Tease me here.

265
00:18:51,146 --> 00:18:55,086
There's nothing more revolting than the complicated affection...

266
00:18:55,086 --> 00:18:57,266
Of someone you're completely disinterested in.

267
00:18:58,266 --> 00:18:58,666
Whoa.

268
00:19:06,666 --> 00:19:07,526
Damn it.

269
00:19:07,826 --> 00:19:08,426
Boomerang.

270
00:19:09,046 --> 00:19:10,066
At that moment.

271
00:19:11,046 --> 00:19:16,506
I had no answer.

272
00:19:17,606 --> 00:19:19,446
I couldn't completely let go.

273
00:19:21,446 --> 00:19:22,946
I don't mean Mugi.

274
00:19:24,946 --> 00:19:26,166
I mean brother.

275
00:19:28,166 --> 00:19:30,186
The brother I was seeing...

276
00:19:30,186 --> 00:19:32,166
Through Mugi.

277
00:19:32,166 --> 00:19:32,726
That's why I...

278
00:19:32,726 --> 00:19:43,366
I'm surprised you came back here.

279
00:19:49,366 --> 00:19:51,006
I didn't think that you would bother.

280
00:19:51,006 --> 00:20:06,706
If you want, we can say that we're dating.

281
00:20:07,386 --> 00:20:07,866
What?

282
00:20:08,286 --> 00:20:10,586
We will both be able to depend on each other.

283
00:20:10,966 --> 00:20:11,586
If needed.

284
00:20:12,066 --> 00:20:15,826
You sure you won't fall in love with me and push your affections on both of us?

285
00:20:15,826 --> 00:20:16,786
I won't.

286
00:20:16,786 --> 00:20:17,886
I promise you.

287
00:20:18,406 --> 00:20:19,906
You're completely not my type.

288
00:20:23,006 --> 00:20:24,166
You're not mine.

289
00:20:24,166 --> 00:20:32,566
And so we made a pact that neither of us would ever fall in love with the other one.

290
00:20:32,566 --> 00:20:37,666
And if one of us makes it with the person we really love, our relationship ends.

291
00:20:37,666 --> 00:20:42,606
In other words, you can have everything but my feelings.

292
00:20:42,966 --> 00:20:43,646
That's the deal.

293
00:20:43,646 --> 00:20:50,566
So I was thinking, does that basically make us friends with benefits?

294
00:20:50,886 --> 00:20:51,626
No, no.

295
00:20:52,066 --> 00:20:52,286
Hmm?

296
00:20:52,986 --> 00:20:53,826
Not at all.

297
00:20:54,566 --> 00:20:55,706
We didn't do it.

298
00:20:56,606 --> 00:20:57,906
And we probably never will.

299
00:21:00,866 --> 00:21:01,386
Yeah?

300
00:21:04,486 --> 00:21:08,666
If one of us is feeling lonely, what's wrong with wanting the other to hold you?

301
00:21:09,266 --> 00:21:12,166
Is that because I'm a virgin and you're scared to deflower me?

302
00:21:12,166 --> 00:21:12,666
Huh?

303
00:21:12,886 --> 00:21:14,126
Where did you get that idea?

304
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:18,066
You'll see in the end.

305
00:21:19,406 --> 00:21:21,066
Our scum's wish will come true.

